Task 1: Deploy Blue and Green Environments
Step 1: Create Application Versions
Create two versions of a simple web application.

Blue Version (v1.0):

mkdir -p ~/blue-green-lab/blue
cd ~/blue-green-lab/blue

cat > index.html << 'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Blue Version</title></head>
<body style="background-color: #4A90E2; color: white; text-align: center; padding: 50px;">
    <h1>Application Version 1.0 - BLUE</h1>
    <p>Current Environment: Production</p>
    <p>Deployment Time: <!-- TODO: Add timestamp --></p>
</body>
</html>
EOF
Green Version (v2.0):

mkdir -p ~/blue-green-lab/green
cd ~/blue-green-lab/green

cat > index.html << 'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Green Version</title></head>
<body style="background-color: #50C878; color: white; text-align: center; padding: 50px;">
    <h1>Application Version 2.0 - GREEN</h1>
    <p>Current Environment: Staging</p>
    <p>New Features: Enhanced UI, Performance Improvements</p>
</body>
</html>
EOF
Step 2: Create Dockerfiles
Blue Dockerfile:

cd ~/blue-green-lab/blue

cat > Dockerfile << 'EOF'
FROM nginx:alpine
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
EXPOSE 80
EOF
Green Dockerfile:

cd ~/blue-green-lab/green

cat > Dockerfile << 'EOF'
FROM nginx:alpine
COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
EXPOSE 80
EOF
Step 3: Build and Run Both Environments
# Build Blue image
cd ~/blue-green-lab/blue
docker build -t app-blue:1.0 .

# Build Green image
cd ~/blue-green-lab/green
docker build -t app-green:2.0 .

# Run Blue container (production - port 8080)
docker run -d --name blue-app -p 8080:80 app-blue:1.0

# Run Green container (staging - port 8081)
docker run -d --name green-app -p 8081:80 app-green:2.0

# Verify both containers are running
docker ps
Step 4: Test Both Environments
# Test Blue environment
curl http://localhost:8080

# Test Green environment
curl http://localhost:8081
Expected Output: You should see HTML content from both versions with different background colors mentioned.

Task 2: Configure Traffic Switching with Nginx
Step 1: Create Nginx Configuration Template
cd ~/blue-green-lab

cat > nginx-config-template.conf << 'EOF'
upstream backend {
    # TODO: Configure upstream server
    # Syntax: server <host>:<port>;
    server localhost:_____;
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name localhost;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://backend;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }

    location /health {
        access_log off;
        return 200 "healthy\n";
        add_header Content-Type text/plain;
    }
}
EOF
Step 2: Implement Blue Configuration
Complete the configuration to route traffic to Blue environment:

cat > /tmp/blue-green-nginx.conf << 'EOF'
upstream backend {
    server localhost:8080;  # Blue environment
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name localhost;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://backend;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    }

    location /health {
        access_log off;
        return 200 "healthy\n";
        add_header Content-Type text/plain;
    }
}
EOF

# Apply configuration
sudo cp /tmp/blue-green-nginx.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/blue-green
sudo ln -sf /etc/nginx/sites-available/blue-green /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo rm -f /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default

# Test and reload
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx
