Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: Nginx configuration test fails

# Check syntax errors
sudo nginx -t

# View detailed error logs
sudo tail -f /var/log/nginx/error.log
Issue: Cannot access application

# Verify containers are running
docker ps -a

# Check container logs
docker logs blue-app
docker logs green-app

# Verify port bindings
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep -E "8080|8081|80"
Issue: Permission denied errors

# Ensure user is in docker group
groups $USER

# If not, re-login or use:
newgrp docker
Conclusion
You have successfully implemented a blue-green deployment strategy using Docker and Nginx. This approach enables:

Zero-downtime deployments: Traffic switches instantly between versions
Easy rollback: Revert to previous version in seconds
Safe testing: New version runs in parallel before going live
Production confidence: Test green environment before switching traffic
Key Takeaways:

Blue-green deployments maintain two identical production environments
Load balancers/reverse proxies enable instant traffic switching
This pattern is fundamental for continuous deployment pipelines
The same principles apply to cloud platforms and container orchestration systems
